# 13(a) Automated Web Application Deployment Using Jenkins
Automated Web Application Deployment Using Jenkins
You are working as a developer in a college software team. Your team has developed a simple
Student Result Web Application using: HTML/CSS/JavaScript for the frontend ,Git for version control ,Jenkins for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment ,A local HTTP server for hosting the application. Perform development of CI/CD Workflow and show the result

## Aim

To implement a simple CI/CD workflow using **Git, Jenkins, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and a local HTTP server**.

## Requirements

* Git/GitHub
* Jenkins
* Python
* VS Code

---

## Step 1: Create the web project

Create a GitHub repository:

```text
student-result-web
```

Clone it:

```powershell
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/student-result-web.git
cd student-result-web
```

---

## Step 2: Create `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Student Result</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Student Result Web Application</h1>
    <p>Deployment successful using Jenkins!</p>
</body>
</html>
```

